<title>ITALY: Mediaset's Publitalia says 96 profit up.</title>
<headline>Mediaset's Publitalia says 96 profit up.</headline>
<dateline>MILAN 1997-03-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ending December 31</p>
<p>(In billion lire unless stated)</p>
<p>    Net profit				   45 vs 172 million</p>
<p>    Pretax profit			   112.3 vs 21.3</p>
<p>    operating profit			129.5 vs 83.6</p>
<p>Gross revenues from sale of advertising space</p>
<p>						  3,272 vs 3,082.9</p>
<p>Net revenues from sale of advertising space</p>
<p>						2,821.1 vs 2,674.2</p>
<p>Gross revenues from television advertising</p>
<p>						  3,240 vs 3,035</p>
<p>Net revenues from television advertising</p>
<p>						2,789.3 vs no comparison</p>
<p>				 Net liquidity  177 vs 459 debt</p>
<p>		     Net financial charges 10.8 vs 65.8</p>
<p>Note - The company said in a statement it estimated revenue from advertising would be up around 10 percent in the first quarter. -- Milan newsroom +392 66129450</p>
</text>
